"""Editorial question designs for radio/audio history and podcasting."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


RADIO = """history_origins|How a Radio Service Began|Which licensing, technology, and audience needs shaped one station?|Compare dated applications, schedules, equipment, and local context.
famous_examples|A Landmark Broadcast Reheard|Why did one recorded broadcast matter to its original listeners?|Compare surviving audio, contemporary response, reach estimates, and later retellings.
hidden_stories|Voices Behind the Microphone|Whose engineering, transcription, translation, and field work was uncredited?|Use production files and attributed crew accounts.
beginner_explainers|From Sound to Broadcast|Which stages carry one program from recording to a listener?|Map microphone, editing, transmission, reception, and archival copy at a high level.
advanced_concepts|What a Recording Omits|How can a surviving recording differ from the original listening event?|Compare edits, transmission context, reception conditions, and archive provenance.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Missing Radio Program|What can be known when a broadcast itself did not survive?|Compare scripts, listings, press accounts, and disputed recollections.
technology_innovation|A Change in Audio Format|How did tape, digital editing, or streaming alter a station's work?|Compare production cost, portability, preservation, and audience access.
people_personalities|Who Shaped the Voice?|How did presenter, producer, writer, and engineer shape one program?|Trace scripts, cues, credits, and attributed interviews.
major_events|Radio During a Crisis|How did one broadcaster verify and deliver information during a dated event?|Compare recordings, bulletins, corrections, and access limits.
how_it_works|A Live Radio Program|How do teams coordinate a broadcast's segments and timing?|Follow one documented rundown, roles, contingency, and final recording.
rise_fall|A Station Changes Format|Why did one broadcaster abandon or restore a format?|Compare audience measurement, funding, regulation, and community response.
then_vs_now|One Program Across Audio Eras|How did production, distribution, and listening change?|Compare dated versions, equipment, scheduling, and access.
future_developments|Preserving a Radio Archive|What should an archive retain when transferring fragile recordings?|Review audio, metadata, carrier history, rights, and access plans.
myths_vs_facts|The Broadcast Panic Story|Does a famous claim about listener reaction match contemporary evidence?|Check audience size, press accounts, letters, and later embellishment.
documentary_stories|One Broadcast's Record|How did an audio program move from script to transmission and archive?|Build a dated chain of production, distribution, reception, and reuse.
creative_brief|Why a Program Was Commissioned|Which audience and service aim guided one radio production?|Compare brief, budget, schedule, and finished episode.
materials_and_tools|The Sound of the Studio|How did microphones, rooms, and recording media shape one program?|Use technical records and audio comparison without assuming intent.
process_breakdown|A Segment From Draft to Air|What changed between script, rehearsal, recording, and broadcast?|Compare surviving versions and producer notes.
composition_choice|Sound and Silence|How did voice, ambience, music, and silence guide one story?|Analyze a bounded sequence and source rights.
collaborative_authorship|Who Wrote the Radio Moment?|How did script, performance, sound design, and editing combine?|Compare credits, drafts, recordings, and recollections.
adaptation_across_media|A Story Becomes Radio|What changed when a text or stage work became audio?|Compare structure, narration, rights, and listening experience.
audience_reception|What Listeners Heard|What can letters, ratings, and oral histories reveal about reception?|Check sample, period, selection, and differing responses.
cultural_context|A Broadcast in Its Community|How did one program serve or exclude local language and culture?|Compare schedule, content, access, and community accounts.
preservation_restoration|Restoring a Recording|Which transfer choices reveal or obscure the original sound?|Document carrier, playback, noise treatment, and preservation master.
rights_and_attribution|Who May Replay the Audio?|Which performer, music, writer, and broadcaster rights apply to a program?|Check dated agreements and current jurisdiction before reuse.
style_comparison|Two Versions of a Radio Format|How do pacing, voice, and sound choices differ?|Compare matched segments within production and audience context.
creative_failure|A Broadcast That Missed Its Aim|Which records show why one program failed to reach its stated audience?|Compare brief, transmission, response, and alternative explanations.
field_textual_form|Reading a Radio Script|How does a script encode sound, timing, and voice?|Compare cues and text with a surviving recording.
field_performance_choice|Voice and Delivery|How did a presenter's pacing or emphasis change meaning?|Analyze one recording with script and production context.
field_audience_history|Who Could Tune In?|How did coverage, receivers, language, and schedules shape audience?|Use dated service maps, surveys, and listener accounts.
field_translation_or_adaptation|One Broadcast in Two Languages|What changed in a translated audio version?|Compare wording, performance, timing, rights, and reception.
field_critical_reception|A Program Reassessed|Why did later critics hear one broadcast differently?|Compare contemporary reviews with new archives and current scholarship."""


PODCAST = """history_origins|Where Podcast Distribution Began|How did feeds and portable players enable one early show?|Trace dated feed, files, platform support, and creator accounts.
famous_examples|A Breakout Podcast Tested|Which evidence explains one show's reported success?|Compare downloads, distribution, promotion, press, and measurement limits.
hidden_stories|Work Behind the Host|Who researches, books, edits, transcribes, and moderates an episode?|Use credits, budgets, and attributed production accounts.
beginner_explainers|How a Podcast Reaches a Listener|What roles do hosting, RSS, directories, and apps play?|Follow one published episode through feed, enclosure, index, and playback.
advanced_concepts|Downloads Are Not Listeners|What does a podcast download metric actually count?|Check methodology, deduplication, partial requests, and cross-platform gaps.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Did Audience Numbers Change?|Which distribution or measurement changes fit a reported jump?|Compare feed, app, campaign, bot filtering, and episode mix.
technology_innovation|Automated Podcast Production|Did one transcription or editing tool improve quality or access?|Compare error rates, human review, privacy, and producer labor.
people_personalities|The Host's Editorial Role|How did a named host shape questions, sourcing, and tone?|Use scripts, interviews, credits, and final audio.
major_events|A Podcast After a Correction|How did one show respond to a documented factual error?|Trace update, feed replacement, notice, transcript, and listener reach.
how_it_works|From Pitch to Published Episode|Which decisions shape a podcast episode at each stage?|Map research, consent, recording, fact-check, edit, rights, feed, and follow-up.
rise_fall|Why a Podcast Stopped|Which factors explain one show's end or relaunch?|Compare funding, workload, audience, rights, and creator statements.
then_vs_now|One Show Across Seasons|How did format, sourcing, sound, and distribution change?|Compare named episodes and production records on the same criteria.
future_developments|A New Podcast Format Pilot|What would show whether a proposed format serves listeners?|Define comprehension, accessibility, retention, cost, and editorial safeguards.
myths_vs_facts|The Viral Podcast Claim|Does a spike in downloads prove a large engaged audience?|Check unique requests, completion evidence, promotion, and timeframe.
documentary_stories|One Episode's Production Trail|How did a published podcast story evolve from first source to correction?|Build a dated record of claims, edits, consent, and follow-up.
creative_brief|An Episode for a Defined Audience|What should one episode help a specific audience understand?|Set question, length, access needs, evidence standard, and takeaway.
materials_and_tools|Choosing a Recording Setup|How do microphone, room, remote link, and backup affect usable speech?|Compare test recordings, accessibility, cost, and reliability.
process_breakdown|The Edit That Changed the Meaning|Where can trimming a conversation remove needed context?|Compare raw consented audio, edit decisions, transcript, and review.
composition_choice|Voice, Music, and Evidence|How do sound choices affect the perceived certainty of a claim?|Analyze one passage and test whether sonic emphasis overstates evidence.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made This Episode?|How are research, reporting, sound design, and hosting credited?|Compare actual work, agreements, bylines, and listener-facing credits.
adaptation_across_media|Audio to Transcript|What is lost or gained when a podcast becomes text or video?|Compare speakers, non-speech audio, visual dependence, and discoverability.
audience_reception|What Listeners Understood|Do reviews and analytics reveal actual comprehension?|Compare consented feedback, representative samples, and metric limits.
cultural_context|A Podcast for a Community|How did language, references, and access shape one show's reception?|Center participants' accounts and avoid treating one audience as uniform.
preservation_restoration|Will the Feed Survive?|What must be saved so an episode remains findable and usable?|Review audio master, transcript, metadata, feed snapshot, rights, and backups.
rights_and_attribution|Who Can Reuse a Clip?|What permissions govern one interview, music bed, or archival excerpt?|Check written terms, local copyright, attribution, and withdrawal conditions.
style_comparison|Interview Versus Narrated Story|How do two podcast formats support the same evidence differently?|Compare sourcing, editing transparency, access, and listener comprehension.
creative_failure|A Pilot That Did Not Work|Why did one episode miss its editorial or audience goal?|Compare brief, production issues, feedback, and measured outcomes.
field_shot_design|When a Podcast Adds Video|Does a visual shot clarify evidence or only decorate the audio?|Compare audio-only and video versions for comprehension and access.
field_production_workflow|A Repeatable Episode Workflow|Which production step prevents the most avoidable errors?|Review version control, fact-checks, consent, deadlines, and corrections.
field_sound_choices|Making Speech Understandable|How do room noise, levels, and mixing affect listener comprehension?|Compare accessible listening tests on different devices.
field_editing_rhythm|Pacing Without Distortion|Can an edit keep a story clear without deleting vital qualifications?|Compare transcript, source context, and listener interpretation.
field_distribution_format|Feed and App Compatibility|Which metadata or audio choices prevent an episode from reaching listeners?|Check current RSS requirements, enclosure, accessibility, and app tests."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("124", "124_radio_audio", RADIO,
                  "Radio and audio history through broadcasts, collaborative production, transmission, listeners, surviving recordings, rights, and preservation.",
                  "surviving audio and scripts, broadcaster schedules and production files, audience and coverage records, contemporary reviews, archive metadata, and attributed crew accounts",
                  "Name program, broadcaster, geography, date, and surviving version. Distinguish original transmission from archival copy, mark gaps, and verify current reuse rights.")
    revise_domain("125", "125_podcasting", PODCAST,
                  "Podcasting through research, consent, recorded sound, editing, accessibility, feed distribution, metrics, rights, and corrections.",
                  "original episodes and transcripts, production and fact-check records, feed and hosting metadata, consent and rights agreements, audience methods, and listener feedback",
                  "Name show, episode, platform, release date, and metric definition. Protect interviewees, verify claims and rights, and distinguish downloads from people or comprehension.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
